.SS recovery\-os status
Print the
.B "RECOVERY OS"
report section for every
.B "role = \(dqmirror\(dq"
target, in config order: each one that is mounted at its configured mount
point is read as for
.BR "recovery\-os inspect" ,
with
.I <mount>/@
as the root; the others print
.BR "not mounted" .
.B backup\-run.sh
runs it after btrbk, while the targets are mounted, and records the result as
an operation: exit 0 is OK (the detail reads
.BR "nothing needs attention" ,
naming any mirror that was not mounted),
exit 1 is WARN, its detail saying
.BR stale ,
.B btrbk may run at boot
or both, as the section's
.B Result
and
.B WARNING
rows show (the report status reads
.BR "COMPLETED WITH WARNINGS" ,
the run is still recorded as a success), anything else is FAIL. The script
bounds the command with
.B timeout
(300 s, then KILL after 10 s more); a check that times out is a FAIL, and the
run goes on to unmount and report.
